<span id="S3.F1.pic1.6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.F1.picx.x.x.x" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Longitudinal Aggregation</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 391.73 -9.31)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:11.88em;--ltx-fo-height:0.56em;--ltx-fo-depth:3.76em;font-size:10pt;" height="59.65" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="164.39"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S3.F1.pic1.7" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_top" style="width:11.88em;">
<span id="S3.F1.pic1.7.1" class="ltx_p"></span>
<span id="S3.F1.pic1.7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.F1.picx.x.x.x" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Survival &amp; churn</span></span>
<span id="S3.F1.pic1.7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.F1.picx.x.x.x" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">HHI, Top-<math id="S3.F1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> shares</span></span>
<span id="S3.F1.pic1.7.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.F1.picx.x.x.x" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Monthly evolution</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#B2B2B2;--ltx-fill-color:#F5F5F7;" fill="#F5F5F7" stroke="#B2B2B2" stroke-width="0.6pt"><path d="M 619.47 30.51 L 557.7 30.51 C 554.64 30.51 552.17 28.03 552.17 24.98 L 552.17 -24.98 C 552.17 -28.03 554.64 -30.51 557.7 -30.51 L 619.47 -30.51 C 622.52 -30.51 625 -28.03 625 -24.98 L 625 24.98 C 625 28.03 622.52 30.51 619.47 30.51 Z M 552.17 -30.51"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.6pt" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 556.1 13.15)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:5.52em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:2.65em;font-size:10pt;" height="47.05" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="76.38"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S3.F1.pic1.8" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_top" style="width:5.52em;">
<span id="S3.F1.pic1.8.1" class="ltx_p"></span>
<span id="S3.F1.pic1.8.2" class="ltx_inline-block fas fa-file" aria-hidden="true">
</span>
<span id="S3.F1.pic1.8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.F1.picx.x.x.x" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#6D6D6D;">*</span><span id="S3.F1.picx.x.x.x" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> <span id="S3.F1.pic1.8.3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Outputs</span></span></span>
<span id="S3.F1.pic1.8.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.F1.picx.x.x.x" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">§<a href="#S4" title="4. Temporal Dynamics ‣ Ollama in the Wild: A Longitudinal Measurement of Exposed Ollama LLM Endpoints at Internet Scale" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>–<a href="#S7" title="7. Operational Characterization ‣ Ollama in the Wild: A Longitudinal Measurement of Exposed Ollama LLM Endpoints at Internet Scale" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a></span></span>
<span id="S3.F1.pic1.8.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.F1.picx.x.x.x" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">findings</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#7D7D7D;" stroke="#7D7D7D" stroke-width="1.1pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 36.42 0 L 42.52 0"></path><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#7D7D7D;" fill="#7D7D7D" stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 38.39 0)"><path d="M 9.74 0 L 2.49 2.63 L 4.51 0 L 2.49 -2.63 Z"></path></g></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#7D7D7D;" stroke="#7D7D7D" stroke-width="1.1pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 203.74 0 L 209.84 0"></path><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#7D7D7D;" fill="#7D7D7D" stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 205.71 0)"><path d="M 9.74 0 L 2.49 2.63 L 4.51 0 L 2.49 -2.63 Z"></path></g></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#7D7D7D;" stroke="#7D7D7D" stroke-width="1.1pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 371.06 0 L 377.16 0"></path><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#7D7D7D;" fill="#7D7D7D" stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 373.03 0)"><path d="M 9.74 0 L 2.49 2.63 L 4.51 0 L 2.49 -2.63 Z"></path></g></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#7D7D7D;" stroke="#7D7D7D" stroke-width="1.1pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 538.39 0 L 544.49 0"></path><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#7D7D7D;" fill="#7D7D7D" stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 540.35 0)"><path d="M 9.74 0 L 2.49 2.63 L 4.51 0 L 2.49 -2.63 Z"></path></g></g></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S3.F1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 1</span>. </span><span id="S3.F1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">End-to-end measurement and analysis pipeline.<span id="S3.F1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
The pipeline consists of daily active probing, per-IP enrichment, and longitudinal aggregation stages.
Inputs are public IPv4 port 11434 scans; outputs support the analyses in <a href="#S4" title="4. Temporal Dynamics ‣ Ollama in the Wild: A Longitudinal Measurement of Exposed Ollama LLM Endpoints at Internet Scale" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>–<a href="#S7" title="7. Operational Characterization ‣ Ollama in the Wild: A Longitudinal Measurement of Exposed Ollama LLM Endpoints at Internet Scale" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>.</span></span><span id="acmlabel1" class="ltx_acm_description ltx_centering ltx_nodisplay">Left-to-right flow diagram of the measurement pipeline.
An input block labeled Public IPv4 port 11434 feeds into three equally-sized colored stage boxes, each with a compact colored header band placing the icon, circled stage number, and stage title on one line, and a white body listing three methods for that stage.
Simple arrows connect the stages to a closing outputs block that points at Sections 4 to 7.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.1. </span>Observation Setup</h3>

<div id="S3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We define an <em id="S3.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">exposed endpoint</em> as a distinct public IPv4 address on TCP/11434 that returns the expected Ollama API response from our measurement vantage point.
We observe these endpoints through daily active probing of port 11434 across the full IPv4 address space from the same measurement vantage point.
Each daily sweep uses XMap <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li, 2025</a>)</cite>, a fast Internet-wide network scanner, to enumerate IPs that complete a TCP connection and return a valid Ollama HTTP response.
For each responsive IP, we issue a follow-up request to the <span id="S3.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">/api/tags</span> endpoint and record the model inventory and HTTP-level metadata; a separate <span id="S3.SS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">/api/version</span> request records the Ollama version string, with version probing beginning on 2025-02-23.
The observation window spans 365 calendar days from 2025-02-14 to 2026-02-13.
Three days have no scan output (2025-02-15, 2025-05-08, 2025-09-27) because of unrecoverable collection failures and are therefore absent from the observed-day dataset.
Among the remaining 362 observed days, 11 exhibit transient low-coverage anomalies caused by upstream network fluctuations or collection failures (2025-02-20, 2025-04-10–13, 2025-04-19–23, 2026-02-11), manifesting as short-term metric drops.
We flag an observed day as <em id="S3.SS1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">low-coverage</em> when its daily alive count falls below 50% of its 30-day rolling median or its daily unique model count falls below 30% of its own 30-day rolling median.
These 11 days remain in the dataset and contribute to aggregate and survival analyses, but we exclude them from several rate-based metrics, including daily churn and correlation calculations.
In the corresponding time-series figures, the three missing dates and 11 low-coverage dates are marked by grey vertical bands and line gaps.
The resulting dataset covers 362 of the 365 calendar days (99.2%) and contains approximately 4.8 million IP<math id="S3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math>day observations.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2. </span>Measurement Pipeline</h3>

<figure id="S3.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S3.T2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 2</span>. </span><span id="S3.T2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Measurement and enrichment coverage.</span></figcaption>
<table id="S3.T2.5" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="S3.T2.5.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S3.Tx.x.x.x" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt">Metric</td>
<td id="S3.Tx.x.x.x" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_tt">Value</td></tr>
<tr id="S3.T2.5.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S3.Tx.x.x.x" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">Observation window</td>
<td id="S3.Tx.x.x.x" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_t">2025-02-14 to 2026-02-13</td></tr>
<tr id="S3.T2.5.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S3.Tx.x.x.x" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Span (calendar days)</td>
<td id="S3.Tx.x.x.x" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right">365</td></tr>
<tr id="S3.T2.5.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S3.Tx.x.x.x" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Observed days (with data)</td>
<td id="S3.Tx.x.x.x" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right">362</td></tr>
<tr id="S3.T2.5.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S3.Tx.x.x.x" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Cumulative exposed IPs</td>
<td id="S3.Tx.x.x.x" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right">152,137</td></tr>
<tr id="S3.T2.5.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S3.Tx.x.x.x" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Latest daily alive count</td>
<td id="S3.Tx.x.x.x" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right">16,059</td></tr>
<tr id="S3.T2.5.7" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S3.Tx.x.x.x" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Geo enrichment matched</td>
<td id="S3.Tx.x.x.x" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right">99.84% (151,886)</td></tr>
<tr id="S3.T2.5.8" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S3.Tx.x.x.x" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">ASN matched</td>
<td id="S3.Tx.x.x.x" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right">99.53% (151,427)</td></tr>
<tr id="S3.T2.5.9" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S3.Tx.x.x.x" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">PTR record present</td>
<td id="S3.Tx.x.x.x" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right">43.22% (65,747)</td></tr>
<tr id="S3.T2.5.10" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S3.Tx.x.x.x" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">TLS handshake successful</td>
<td id="S3.Tx.x.x.x" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb">14.44% (21,963)</td></tr>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our end-to-end measurement and analysis pipeline (<a href="#acmlabel1" title="In 3. Measurement Design ‣ Ollama in the Wild: A Longitudinal Measurement of Exposed Ollama LLM Endpoints at Internet Scale" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) is organized into three stages:</p>
<ol id="S3.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Daily active probing.</span>
We use XMap <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li, 2025</a>)</cite> to identify hosts responding on port 11434 via daily IPv4 sweeps, and for each responsive IP we issue HTTP requests to <span id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">/api/tags</span> and <span id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">/api/version</span> to capture the model inventory and Ollama version string.
We count each responsive IP once per day and aggregate model identifiers and version strings into daily frequency tables.
This step yields 362 alive-IP snapshots with paired per-day model caches.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Enrichment.</span>
After completing the observation window, we enrich each unique observed IP once in three passes: (i) GeoIP and ASN attribution with MaxMind GeoLite2 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">MaxMind, 2024</a>)</cite>, achieving a 99.84% match rate; (ii) PTR reverse DNS with forward A/AAAA verification; and (iii) a TLS handshake attempt on port 443 as a co-located host observation.
The resulting GeoIP/ASN labels and PTR/TLS observations are joined to the longitudinal dataset by IP.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Longitudinal aggregation.</span>
We reduce the enriched corpus to longitudinal metrics that drive <a href="#S4" title="4. Temporal Dynamics ‣ Ollama in the Wild: A Longitudinal Measurement of Exposed Ollama LLM Endpoints at Internet Scale" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sections</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> to <a href="#S7" title="7. Operational Characterization ‣ Ollama in the Wild: A Longitudinal Measurement of Exposed Ollama LLM Endpoints at Internet Scale" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>: survival distributions for IPs, models, and versions; daily new and retired IP churn; and country/region- and ASN-level concentration curves with Top-<math id="S3.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> shares and HHI.
These metrics are defined formally in the next subsection.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#S3.T2" title="In 3.2. Measurement Pipeline ‣ 3. Measurement Design ‣ Ollama in the Wild: A Longitudinal Measurement of Exposed Ollama LLM Endpoints at Internet Scale" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> summarizes the pipeline’s coverage and quality metrics.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.3. </span>Metrics and Survival Analysis</h3>

<div id="S3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Three metric families support the analyses in <a href="#S4" title="4. Temporal Dynamics ‣ Ollama in the Wild: A Longitudinal Measurement of Exposed Ollama LLM Endpoints at Internet Scale" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sections</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> to <a href="#S7" title="7. Operational Characterization ‣ Ollama in the Wild: A Longitudinal Measurement of Exposed Ollama LLM Endpoints at Internet Scale" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>:</p>
<ul id="S3.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S3.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Daily-level metrics.</span>
<em id="S3.I2.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Daily alive count</em> is the number of endpoints responding on a given date; <em id="S3.I2.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">cumulative alive count</em> is the cumulative distinct IPs observed up to that date; <em id="S3.I2.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">daily unique model count</em> and <em id="S3.I2.i1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">daily unique version count</em> capture daily software diversity.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Survival metrics.</span>
Following the survival-analytic framing of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kleinbaum and Klein, 2012</a>)</cite>, for each entity (IP, model, version) we compute <em id="S3.I2.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">active days</em> (number of days observed), <em id="S3.I2.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">span coverage</em> (active days divided by calendar span), and <em id="S3.I2.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">longest streak</em> (maximum consecutive days observed), and summarize their distributions as CDFs and percentiles (P50, P90, P99).
Measurements are taken once per day, so active days count the dates on which an entity is observed.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Concentration metrics.</span>
Using MaxMind’s GeoLite2 City and ASN databases <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">MaxMind, 2024</a>)</cite>, we analyze geographic and infrastructural concentration via IP-day-weighted top-<math id="S3.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> shares and the Herfindahl–Hirschman Index (HHI) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rhoades, 1993</a>)</cite>.
An IP observed on <math id="S3.I2.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> days contributes <math id="S3.I2.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> observations to its mapped country/region and ASN.
HHI is the sum of squared shares (<math id="S3.I2.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum s_{i}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum s_{i}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>) and is conventionally interpreted as low below 0.15, moderate at 0.15–0.25, and high above 0.25.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The remaining sections are organized as follows: <a href="#S4" title="4. Temporal Dynamics ‣ Ollama in the Wild: A Longitudinal Measurement of Exposed Ollama LLM Endpoints at Internet Scale" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> examines temporal dynamics; <a href="#S5" title="5. Software Ecosystem Evolution ‣ Ollama in the Wild: A Longitudinal Measurement of Exposed Ollama LLM Endpoints at Internet Scale" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> analyzes software ecosystem evolution; <a href="#S6" title="6. Geographic and Infrastructure Concentration ‣ Ollama in the Wild: A Longitudinal Measurement of Exposed Ollama LLM Endpoints at Internet Scale" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> examines geographic and infrastructure concentration; <a href="#S7" title="7. Operational Characterization ‣ Ollama in the Wild: A Longitudinal Measurement of Exposed Ollama LLM Endpoints at Internet Scale" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> presents our operational characterization; <a href="#S8" title="8. Discussion ‣ Ollama in the Wild: A Longitudinal Measurement of Exposed Ollama LLM Endpoints at Internet Scale" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> discusses the findings; and <a href="#S9" title="9. Conclusion ‣ Ollama in the Wild: A Longitudinal Measurement of Exposed Ollama LLM Endpoints at Internet Scale" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> concludes the paper.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4. </span>Temporal Dynamics</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we address several fundamental questions about exposed Ollama services, providing a basic understanding of their scale, persistence, and changes over time.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.F2" class="ltx_figure" aria-describedby="acmlabel2">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S4.F2.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2609.07115v1/fig_exposure_combined.svg" id="S4.F2.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/214;" width="476" height="214"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S4.F2.sf1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a)</span> </span><span id="S4.F2.sf1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Daily exposure and cumulative IP growth.</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S4.F2.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2609.07115v1/fig_ip_churn.svg" id="S4.F2.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/204;" width="476" height="204"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S4.F2.sf2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(b)</span> </span><span id="S4.F2.sf2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Daily IP churn (7-day moving average).</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S4.F2.sf3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2609.07115v1/fig_ip_survival_cdf.svg" id="S4.F2.sf3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/169;" width="476" height="169"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S4.F2.sf3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(c)</span> </span><span id="S4.F2.sf3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">CDF of observed IP active days.</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S4.F2.sf4" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2609.07115v1/fig_ip_survival_buckets.svg" id="S4.F2.sf4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/169;" width="476" height="169"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S4.F2.sf4.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(d)</span> </span><span id="S4.F2.sf4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">IP distribution by observed active days.</span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S4.F2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 2</span>. </span><span id="S4.F2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Temporal dynamics overview.<span id="S4.F2.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
(a) Daily alive-IP count (navy, left axis) and cumulative IP discovery (orange, right axis).
(b) Daily churn as 7-day moving averages of new and retired IPs.
(c) CDF of observed IP active days with P50, P90, and P99 markers.
(d) Number and percentage of IPs grouped by the number of days on which they were observed.</span></span><span id="acmlabel2" class="ltx_acm_description ltx_centering ltx_nodisplay">2x2 panel figure showing temporal dynamics: daily exposure and cumulative growth, daily IP churn, an IP active-day CDF, and a bar chart showing the number of IPs in six observed active-day ranges.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1. </span>Exposure Scale and Trend</h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first measure the daily size of the exposed Ollama surface and how it changes over the year (<a href="#acmlabel2" title="In 4. Temporal Dynamics ‣ Ollama in the Wild: A Longitudinal Measurement of Exposed Ollama LLM Endpoints at Internet Scale" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>(a)).
Starting from 10,473 on 2025-02-14, active IPs surge 60% to a peak of 16,821 on 2025-04-25.
The count then declines to <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\sim}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\sim}</annotation></semantics></math>11,500 by 2025-07, a 32% drop from the peak.
Finally, from 2025-Q4, it climbs gradually back above 15,000, settling at 16,059 on the final observation day (2026-02-13).
Across all 362 days, the mean is 13,254 (median 13,160, std 2,139).</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The cumulative curve (<a href="#acmlabel2" title="In 4. Temporal Dynamics ‣ Ollama in the Wild: A Longitudinal Measurement of Exposed Ollama LLM Endpoints at Internet Scale" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>(a), right axis, orange) reaches 152,137 unique IPs, with a cumulative-to-active ratio of 9.47: historically exposed nodes outnumber currently active ones by nearly an order of magnitude.
New IPs continually join the surface, but the 9.5<math id="S4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> gap between cumulative and active means that most endpoints that have ever been exposed are no longer active, consistent with a high-churn population in which most IPs are short-lived.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2. </span>IP Survival Analysis</h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">IP-level persistence separates short-lived exposure from endpoints that remain reachable for months (<a href="#acmlabel2" title="In 4. Temporal Dynamics ‣ Ollama in the Wild: A Longitudinal Measurement of Exposed Ollama LLM Endpoints at Internet Scale" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>(c,d)).
26.4% of all 152,137 cumulative IPs are observed on exactly one day (i.e., within a single 24-hour observation interval), consistent with short-lived CI/CD pipelines, spot instances, or one-off deployments.
At the far end, 10.3% are observed on 90 or more days and 4.4% (6,619 IPs) are observed on <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≥</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq</annotation></semantics></math>180 days; the longest-lived IPs appear on 358 out of 362 days (98.9% coverage), with continuous streaks reaching 141 days.
The median survival is 5 days (P50) and the 90th percentile reaches 92 days.
The key structural pattern is a large one-day spike followed by a persistent survivor population; our later operational analysis shows that these lifetime groups map onto different cloud and hosting profiles (<a href="#S7" title="7. Operational Characterization ‣ Ollama in the Wild: A Longitudinal Measurement of Exposed Ollama LLM Endpoints at Internet Scale" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.3. </span>Daily Churn</h3>

<div id="S4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Daily arrivals and departures continually refresh the exposure surface.
Excluding the first observation day and all day-to-day transitions involving missing or low-coverage days, the dataset exhibits an average daily IP churn of 775 new IPs and 761 retired IPs (<a href="#acmlabel2" title="In 4. Temporal Dynamics ‣ Ollama in the Wild: A Longitudinal Measurement of Exposed Ollama LLM Endpoints at Internet Scale" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>(b)).
The daily churn rate of <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\sim}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\sim}</annotation></semantics></math>770 IPs/day represents roughly 5.8% of the mean daily alive population, meaning the surface replaces about 6% of itself every day.
Yet the aggregate count appears stable, demonstrating that aggregate stability masks substantial population turnover.
Taken together, the temporal evidence shows a surface that is large, follows a rise-fall-rise pattern, and is highly dynamic: many IPs disappear after a single day, a smaller core persists for months, and the daily churn that sustains this structure is invisible from aggregate counts alone.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5. </span>Software Ecosystem Evolution</h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we turn from endpoint dynamics to the software ecosystem of exposed Ollama services, examining its diversity, evolution, and maintenance over time.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.F3" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2609.07115v1/fig_diversity_trend.svg" id="S5.F3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/189;" width="476" height="189" aria-label="Dual y-axis line chart showing daily unique model counts on the left axis and daily unique Ollama version counts on the right axis.
Light grey vertical bands indicate low-coverage days excluded from both series."><p>Dual y-axis line chart showing daily unique model counts on the left axis and daily unique Ollama version counts on the right axis.
Light grey vertical bands indicate low-coverage days excluded from both series.</p></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S5.F3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 3</span>. </span><span id="S5.F3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Model and version diversity trend.<span id="S5.F3.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
Dual-axis daily counts of unique models (left axis, blue) and unique Ollama versions (right axis, orange).
Grey vertical bands mark low-coverage days (<a href="#S3" title="3. Measurement Design ‣ Ollama in the Wild: A Longitudinal Measurement of Exposed Ollama LLM Endpoints at Internet Scale" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) on which both series are masked.</span></span><span id="acmlabel3" class="ltx_acm_description ltx_centering ltx_nodisplay">Dual y-axis line chart showing daily unique model counts on the left axis and daily unique Ollama version counts on the right axis.
Light grey vertical bands indicate low-coverage days excluded from both series.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S5.F4" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2609.07115v1/fig_monthly_heatmap.svg" id="S5.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/134;" width="476" height="134" aria-label="Line chart of daily endpoint counts for the global top-10 deployed Ollama models, with a top ribbon showing the highest-count model within this set in each month."><p>Line chart of daily endpoint counts for the global top-10 deployed Ollama models, with a top ribbon showing the highest-count model within this set in each month.</p></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S5.F4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 4</span>. </span><span id="S5.F4.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Daily model-count evolution.<span id="S5.F4.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
Daily endpoint counts for the global top-10 models over the measurement window.
The top ribbon marks the highest-count model in each month.
Grey bands mark low-coverage days excluded from the daily series.</span></span><span id="acmlabel4" class="ltx_acm_description ltx_centering ltx_nodisplay">Line chart of daily endpoint counts for the global top-10 deployed Ollama models, with a top ribbon showing the highest-count model within this set in each month.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S5.F5" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2609.07115v1/fig_version_heatmap.svg" id="S5.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/125;" width="476" height="125" aria-label="Daily stacked-bar chart of the global top-10 deployed Ollama versions, with the y-axis truncated to 70 percent.
The top ribbon shows the highest-count version within this set in each month.
A hatched grey band on the leftmost 9 days marks the period before /api/version probing started."><p>Daily stacked-bar chart of the global top-10 deployed Ollama versions, with the y-axis truncated to 70 percent.
The top ribbon shows the highest-count version within this set in each month.
A hatched grey band on the leftmost 9 days marks the period before /api/version probing started.</p></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S5.F5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 5</span>. </span><span id="S5.F5.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Daily version-share evolution.<span id="S5.F5.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
Daily shares of the global top-10 Ollama versions among deployments with parseable version data.
The top ribbon marks the highest-count version within the global top-10 in each month.
The hatched region marks the period before version probing began on 2025-02-23.</span></span><span id="acmlabel5" class="ltx_acm_description ltx_centering ltx_nodisplay">Daily stacked-bar chart of the global top-10 deployed Ollama versions, with the y-axis truncated to 70 percent.
The top ribbon shows the highest-count version within this set in each month.
A hatched grey band on the leftmost 9 days marks the period before /api/version probing started.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="S5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.1. </span>Model and Version Diversity</h3>

<div id="S5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We measure how model and version diversity change as the exposed population grows (<a href="#acmlabel3" title="In 5. Software Ecosystem Evolution ‣ Ollama in the Wild: A Longitudinal Measurement of Exposed Ollama LLM Endpoints at Internet Scale" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>).
A daily model count is the number of distinct reported model identifiers on that date, whereas a daily version count is the number of distinct parseable Ollama daemon versions.
These metrics characterize two dimensions of the exposed software ecosystem: deployed model diversity and Ollama version diversity.
Daily unique model counts rise from 1,797 on the first observation day to 5,643 on the final day (<math id="S5.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+214\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>214</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+214\%</annotation></semantics></math>), peaking at 5,654.
Daily unique version counts rise from 112 when version probing began to 182 on the final day (<math id="S5.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+62.5\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>62.5</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+62.5\%</annotation></semantics></math>).
After excluding low-coverage days, both indicators are weakly correlated with exposure scale:</p>
<ul id="S5.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Corr}(\text{daily alive IPs},\text{daily unique models})=0.29" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Corr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>daily alive IPs</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext>daily unique models</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.29</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Corr}(\text{daily alive IPs},\text{daily unique models})=0.29</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Corr}(\text{daily alive IPs},\text{daily unique versions})=0.23" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Corr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>daily alive IPs</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext>daily unique versions</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.23</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Corr}(\text{daily alive IPs},\text{daily unique versions})=0.23</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The version correlation is computed from 2025-02-23, when version probing began.
These results show limited day-to-day co-movement between exposure scale and software diversity.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S5.T3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 3</span>. </span><span id="S5.T3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Top-10 individual models, model families, and Ollama versions by aggregate observation count across the 362-day window.
Counts are weighted IP<math id="S5.T3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math>day occurrences.
Model and family shares are computed against <math id="S5.T3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\text{model}}=18{,}677{,}394" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>18,677,394</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\text{model}}=18{,}677{,}394</annotation></semantics></math>; version shares are computed against <math id="S5.T3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\text{version}}=4{,}402{,}553" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>version</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4,402,553</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\text{version}}=4{,}402{,}553</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></figcaption>
<table id="S5.T3.5" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="S5.T3.5.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.Tx.x.x.x" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;"><span id="S5.T3.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Rank</span></td>
<td id="S5.Tx.x.x.x" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;" colspan="3"><span id="S5.T3.5.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Top-10 Individual Model</span></td>
<td id="S5.Tx.x.x.x" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;" colspan="3"><span id="S5.T3.5.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Top-10 Model Family</span></td>
<td id="S5.Tx.x.x.x" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;" colspan="3"><span id="S5.T3.5.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Top-10 Version</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T3.5.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.Tx.x.x.x" class="ltx_td" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;"></td>
<td id="S5.Tx.x.x.x" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;"><span id="S5.T3.5.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Model</span></td>
