</figure>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Custom domain.</span>
Any PTR-present IP that falls through the five rules above is classified as Custom domain.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">No PTR.</span>
IPs returning no PTR record or an empty response are classified as no-PTR.
This bucket is reported as a seventh class alongside the six PTR-derived categories throughout <a href="#S7" title="7. Operational Characterization ‣ Ollama in the Wild: A Longitudinal Measurement of Exposed Ollama LLM Endpoints at Internet Scale" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>CVE Coverage and Cutoff Selection</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#S5.SS4" title="5.4. CVE Patch Adoption ‣ 5. Software Ecosystem Evolution ‣ Ollama in the Wild: A Longitudinal Measurement of Exposed Ollama LLM Endpoints at Internet Scale" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.4</span></a> selects five version cutoffs for longitudinal analysis from the 21 Ollama daemon CVEs cataloged for analysis.
<a href="#A4.T9" title="In Appendix D CVE Coverage and Cutoff Selection ‣ Ollama in the Wild: A Longitudinal Measurement of Exposed Ollama LLM Endpoints at Internet Scale" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> lists all 21 CVEs with disclosure dates, CVSS scores, fix versions, and their status with respect to our selection criteria.
CVEs are excluded if they (i) have been rejected as duplicates, (ii) affect a population too small for time-series analysis (<math id="A4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>&lt;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;</annotation></semantics></math>5% of version observations), (iii) were disclosed too late in the observation window to yield a meaningful remediation curve, or (iv) have no fix version recorded in NVD.
In the table, “Bundled” marks CVEs that map to an already selected measurable cutoff; they are not counted among the five selected CVEs.
The five cutoffs that pass all criteria span RCE (CVE-2024-37032, CVE-2024-45436), information disclosure (CVE-2024-39719), token exposure (CVE-2025-51471), and authentication bypass (CVE-2025-63389), and their below-cutoff populations range from 7.4% to 85.9% of version observations.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T9" class="ltx_table">

