<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Artifact Availability</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Availability status: partial.</span>
Raw per-IP records (daily alive snapshots, GeoIP-to-IP mappings, per-IP PTR hostnames, and TLS certificate details) are excluded to protect the privacy of exposed hosts.
The accompanying artifact provides (i) the analysis and figure-generation source code, (ii) aggregate and de-identified datasets covering all 362 observed days, and (iii) pre-generated camera-ready figures.
Analyses that require the withheld per-IP records cannot be rerun from the public artifact alone; the corresponding scripts are included to document the processing logic.
The released aggregate data include daily alive counts, country/region- and ASN-level distributions, model and version frequency tables, survival distributions, PTR/TLS probing and CVE patch-adoption summaries.</p>
</div>
</section>
</article>
